🧠 Introduction

Java provides:

✔ Access Modifiers to control visibility
✔ Inner Classes to organize related classes together

👉 These concepts improve code security and structure.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔐 1. Access Modifiers

Access modifiers define where a class, variable, or method can be accessed.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Types of Access Modifiers

| Modifier    | Same Class | Same Package | Subclass | Other Packages      |
| ----------- | ---------- | ------------ | -------- | ------------------- |
| `private`   | ✔          | ❌            | ❌        | ❌                   |
| Default     | ✔          | ✔            | ❌        | ❌                   |
| `protected` | ✔          | ✔            | ✔        | ✔ (via inheritance) |
| `public`    | ✔          | ✔            | ✔        | ✔                   |

---

🔒 private

Accessible only within the same class.

```java id="am1"
class Demo {
    private int value = 10;
}
```

---

📦 Default (Package-Private)

No modifier specified.

```java id="am2"
class Demo {
    int count = 5;
}
```

---

🛡️ protected

Accessible in same package and subclasses.

```java id="am3"
class Parent {
    protected int age = 20;
}
```

---

🌍 public

Accessible from anywhere.

```java id="am4"
public class Test {
    public int data = 100;
}
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧩 2. Inner Classes

An inner class is a class defined inside another class.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Why Use Inner Classes?

✔ Logical grouping
✔ Better encapsulation
✔ Easier access to outer class members

---

🔹 Member Inner Class

```java id="ic1"
class Outer {
    int x = 10;

    class Inner {
        void show() {
            System.out.println(x);
        }
    }
}
```

---

▶️ Creating Inner Class Object

```java id="ic2"
Outer outer = new Outer();
Outer.Inner inner = outer.new Inner();
inner.show();
```

---

🔹 Static Nested Class

```java id="ic3"
class Outer {
    static class Nested {
        void display() {
            System.out.println("Static Nested Class");
        }
    }
}
```

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

▶️ Creating Static Nested Object

```java id="ic4"
Outer.Nested obj = new Outer.Nested();
obj.display();
```

---

🔹 Local Inner Class

Defined inside a method.

```java id="ic5"
void method() {
    class Local {
        void show() {
            System.out.println("Local Inner Class");
        }
    }
}
```

---

🔹 Anonymous Inner Class

Class without a name.

```java id="ic6"
Runnable r = new Runnable() {
    public void run() {
        System.out.println("Running");
    }
};
```

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 Advantages of Inner Classes

✔ Better code organization
✔ Improved encapsulation
✔ Access to outer class members

---

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Incorrect syntax for creating inner objects
❌ Confusing static nested class with member inner class
❌ Using private members outside class

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ Access modifiers control visibility
✔ `private`, default, `protected`, `public`
✔ Inner classes are classes inside another class
✔ Types: member, static nested, local, anonymous

